1c:["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 text-sm text-slate-700 shadow-sm","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Key numbers:"}]," Break-even fee is 1.83% (zero margin) and 2.33% for £50 margin. Effective cost is about 21% annualised, so target firms that cannot get a facility. The expected-loss reserve covers only 0.33% of principal, so diversification is essential. If the platform alone bore all loss, break-even default rate is about 1.7% of invoices.",["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500","children":"Investor return is not promised. It is the invoice discount minus losses. Legal structure (receivable purchase or loan notes) needs an FCA-authorised partner."}]]}]
